A figure that yields no netlist is signalled with \code{\link[cli:cli_abort]{cli::cli_abort()}}
as a condition of class \code{spice_error_pic} (and \code{spice_error}): rpic
rejected it (a syntax error, an unknown label, ...) or it is not
marked \code{spice = 1}. The message carries the figure's \code{line:col}; the
condition's fields \code{line} and \code{column} hold them (\code{NA} when there is
no position), and \code{diagnostics} holds the one diagnostic, of kind
\code{"compile"} or \code{"not-marked"}. An unreadable figure file is a
\code{spice_error_io}, a bad \code{snap} a \code{spice_error_input}.
